@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+QUARANTINED r51 TRIAL — NOT A QUALIFIED HARDWARE RELEASE.
+
+The initial software reboot after r51 installation reached Qualcomm9008.
+After the owner reconnected the phone, r51 booted and native L2/S2
+bootstrap checks passed with unchanged VCTL and programmed1.15V APC.
+The failing stage/cause and repeatable boot remain unqualified.
+r50 has since been restored, normally rebooted and verified.
+
+This source recipe preserves the r51 trial. Separate unpackaged follow-ups
+remove generic PMIC gate callbacks from the always-on SAW CPU rail and
+compute exact APC/MX voltage plans. They are not part of this package and
+have no native voltage-transition qualification. Future first controller
+trials use RAM boot before persistent installation.
+Audio testing remains excluded; host built-in Wi-Fi must not be changed.
+
+Revision r52 source candidate includes all 17 CPU-series patches (22 total
+integration patches), including no-enable correction, voltage planning, MX
+activation, attachment retry and corner mapping. No native r52 trial yet.
+CPR/OPP consumer integration remains incomplete and CPR stays disabled.
+r51 had an unexplained EDL event followed by one successful native bootstrap;
+r50 was restored. First future power-controller trials must use RAM boot.
diff --git a/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-msm8226/README.fx0-dmp b/device/testing/linux-postmarketos-qcom-msm8226/README.fx0-dmp
