@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Fx0 DMP development package preparation
+=======================================
+
+Prepared from pmaports CPU-idle integration 0a5720063, before the later audio
+experiment recipes. The pinned kernel source is 4b800b920c7db82e8012a580a17cc2d8ff9d5e66.
+Four ordered patches reproduce the nine changed files in worktrees/linux-dmp.
+No proprietary DMP firmware is included; firmware remains separately provisioned.
+
+The candidate package is 6.18.59-r47 and uses kernel release 6.18.59-fx0-dmp.
+A fixed release avoids dependence on archive checkout SCM information and keeps
+its module directory separate from both legacy 6.18.59 and the running trial.
+The inherited recipe uses LLVM; the running development trial was built with GCC.
+This recipe therefore requires its own complete build and device qualification.
+
+Validated: shell syntax, all local SHA-512 entries, ordered patch application,
+and exact patched-source comparison to the running candidate source.
+The separate host Clang/CFI build and signed binary-wrapper APK now pass; all
+464 module vermagics and 545 packaged file hashes were checked. This source
+recipe itself has not been built with Alpine abuild. The signed host-built
+binary-wrapper APK is now installed through normal APK hooks. The phone boots
+6.18.59-fx0-dmp with matching installed metadata and taint zero. Boot-image
+readback and lk2nd prefix preservation passed; raw/quaternion, awake arming
+and one RTC suspend also pass. Physical motion-wake qualification is pending
+on this Clang/CFI build; earlier GCC tests do not qualify this image.
+Never change kernel or module inputs during an active 20-cycle wake run.
+Audio testing remains excluded.
+
+Later current-phone result: r49 retains this DMP implementation and adds an
+MSM video-start ordering change. Twenty consecutive physical DMP wakes and a
+matched disabled-SMD motion control pass with zero taint/underruns; owner
+confirms display/touch recovery. Overall battery/overnight, 50-cycle/peripheral
+and false-wake/accuracy gates remain open. See coordination-repo evidence.
